    "__Proof.__  If $B = P^{-1}AP,$ then\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\begin{align*}\n",
    "B - \\lambda I &= P^{-1}AP - \\lambda I \\\\\n",
    "&= P^{-1}AP - \\lambda P^{-1}P \\\\\n",
    "&= P^{-1}(AP-\\lambda P) \\\\\n",
    "&= P^{-1}(A-\\lambda I)P.\n",
    "\\end{align*}$$\n",
    "\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "## Similarity\n",
    "\n",
    ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
    "Now let's construct the characteristic polynomial by taking the determinant:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\begin{align*}\n",
    "\\det(B-\\lambda I) &= \\det[P^{-1}(A-\\lambda I)P] \\\\\n",
    "&= \\det(P^{-1})\\cdot\\det(A-\\lambda I)\\cdot\\det(P),\n",
    "\\end{align*}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "using the fact that the determinant of the product of matrices equals the product of the determinants.\n",
    "\n",
    "<br>\n",
    "\n",
    "Finally, since $\\det(P^{-1})\\cdot\\det(P) = \\det(P^{-1}P) = \\det I = 1,$ we can see that \n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\det(B-\\lambda I) = \\det(A - \\lambda I).$$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "## Warnings\n",
    "\n",
    ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
    "1. The eigenvalues of a matrix with real entries might be complex.\n",
    "\n",
    "__Example.__ Consider the \"rotation by 90 degrees\" matrix:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$A = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "It does not have any real-valued eigenvalues."
